## How this addresses each failure

| Failing test | Root cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `single-m-4755-simple-*` | `mkdir()` strips S_ISUID | Change 2 (chmod restores 04000) |
| `single-m-2755-simple-*` | `mkdir()` strips S_ISGID | Change 2 (chmod restores 02000) |
| `single-m-u+s-simple-*` | Both bugs: parsing gives 04755 (Bug 2), then mkdir strips S_ISUID (Bug 1) | Change 1 fixes parsing to 04777; Change 2 restores S_ISUID |
| `single-m-g+s-simple-*` | Both bugs: parsing gives 02755 (Bug 2), then mkdir strips S_ISGID (Bug 1) | Change 1 fixes parsing to 02777; Change 2 restores S_ISGID |
| `quirk-special-bits` (`-m 4755`) | `mkdir()` strips S_ISUID | Change 2 |
| `rand-ok-039-m-p-nested` (`-m u+s -p`) | Parsing gives 04755 instead of 04777 | Change 1 (the `-p` path already chmods the final dir) |

## Unresolved constraints

None. All 14 failures are addressed by these two changes. No compiler diagnostics are expected (only standard POSIX headers and functions are used; `chmod` is already available via `<sys/stat.h>`).
